Q: Laravel Reverb WebSocket events not received on frontend (403 broadcasting/auth error) A: <p>Make sure you have this in your channels.php:</p>
<pre><code>Broadcast::channel('donor.{id}', function ($user, $id) {
    return (int) $user-&gt;id === (int) $id;
});
</code></pre>

Q: CodeIgniter Query Builder WHERE a column value is greater than another column value A: <p>Have a look at this example from the Codeigniter documentation:</p>

<pre><code>$this-&gt;db-&gt;where('name !=', $name);
$this-&gt;db-&gt;where('id &lt;', $id); 

// Produces: WHERE name != 'Joe' AND id &lt; 45
</code></pre>

<p>It looks as though you may need a space between quantita and >. Try:</p>

<pre><code>$this-&gt;db-&gt;where('quantita &gt;', 'alerts');
</code></pre>

Q: How to populate nested objects simultaneously in ASP.NET A: <p>You need to flatten that DTO and move the generation logic directly into your <code>ToMedicationScheduleFromCreateDto</code> mapper without touching the controller at all.</p>
<pre><code>public class CreateMedicationScheduleDto
{
    public int? UserId { get; set; }
    public int? MedicationId { get; set; }
    public int NumberOfPills { get; set; }
    public int Duration { get; set; }
    public DateOnly StartDate { get; set; }

    public List&lt;TimeOnly&gt; ReminderHours { get; set; } = new(); 
}
</code></pre>
<p>Drop the calendar generation loop right inside that extension method-</p>
<pre><code>public static MedicationSchedule ToMedicationScheduleFromCreateDto(this CreateMedicationScheduleDto dto)
{    
    if (dto.ReminderHours.Count != dto.NumberOfPills)
        throw new ArgumentException($&quot;ReminderHours count ({dto.ReminderHours.Count}) must match NumberOfPills ({dto.NumberOfPills}).&quot;);

    var schedule = new MedicationSchedule
    {
        UserId        = dto.UserId,
        MedicationId  = dto.MedicationId,
        NumberOfPills = dto.NumberOfPills,
        Duration      = dto.Duration,
        StartDate     = dto.StartDate,
        EndDate       = dto.StartDate.AddDays(dto.Duration - 1),
        ReminderPlannings = new List&lt;ReminderPlanning&gt;()
    };

    for (int i = 0; i &lt; dto.Duration; i++)
    {
        var day = dto.StartDate.AddDays(i);
        schedule.ReminderPlannings.Add(new ReminderPlanning
        {
            reminderDay = day,
            dayOfWeek   = day.DayOfWeek.ToString(),
            medicationReminders = dto.ReminderHours
                .Select(h =&gt; new MedicationReminder { ReminderHour = h })
                .ToList()
        });
    }

    return schedule;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Call the API-</p>
<pre><code>{
  &quot;userId&quot;: 1,
  &quot;medicationId&quot;: 12,
  &quot;numberOfPills&quot;: 2,
  &quot;duration&quot;: 30,
  &quot;startDate&quot;: &quot;2026-05-01&quot;,
  &quot;reminderHours&quot;: [
    &quot;08:00:00&quot;,
    &quot;20:00:00&quot;
  ]
}
</code></pre>
<p>Hope this helps!!</p>

Q: How to match patterns AdditionalIncludePaths metaproperty for compilation in Visual Studio A: <p>Instead of <code>ItemDefinitionGroup</code> a <code>PropertyGroup</code> should be built used with <code>%(ClCompile.AdditionalIncludeDirectories)</code>. Item group required &quot;import&quot; of at first by using  <code>IncPaths</code> property, then conditionally include to new <code>AdditionalIncludeDirectories</code> if <code>%(Identity)</code> matches pattern.</p>
<p><code>Directory.Build.targets</code> file (formatted for readability):</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;Project&gt;
  &lt;Target Name=&quot;RemoveAdditionalIncludeTemp&quot; BeforeTargets=&quot;ClCompile&quot;&gt;
    &lt;PropertyGroup&gt;
      &lt;TempList&gt;
          %(ClCompile.AdditionalIncludeDirectories)
      &lt;/TempList&gt;
    &lt;/PropertyGroup&gt;
    &lt;ItemGroup&gt;
      &lt;IncPaths Include=&quot;$(TempList)&quot; /&gt;
      &lt;FilteredPaths Include=&quot;@(IncPaths)&quot; 
                     Condition=&quot;! $([System.String]::
                               Copy('%(Identity)').Contains('$(Temp)'))&quot; /&gt;
      &lt;ClCompile&gt;
        &lt;AdditionalIncludeDirectories&gt;
              &quot;@(FilteredPaths)&quot;
        &lt;/AdditionalIncludeDirectories&gt;
      &lt;/ClCompile&gt;
    &lt;/ItemGroup&gt;
    &lt;!--&lt;Exec Command=&quot;echo $(TempList)&quot; /&gt;--&gt;
  &lt;/Target&gt;

&lt;/Project&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: SELECT rows with a status found in a conditionally built whitelist using CodeIgniter&#39;s query builder A: <p>We are dealing with &quot;magic numbers&quot; here (<code>option_#</code> and status <code>#</code>) and that should be avoided or at least explicitly explained in the codebase. Set up a lookup array as a class-level property to remove reliance on multiple sets of condition blocks.</p>
<p>If the form elements are radio buttons, then zero or one option will be expected. If the form elements are checkboxes, then zero, one, two, or three options will be expected. If more than one, then the mapped values will need to be merged into a flat array then consumed by <code>where_in()</code>. Using <code>where_in()</code> avoids the need to implement logic encapsulating parentheses in the built query.</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>// near the top of your model class...
protected array $optionStatusMap = [
    'option_1' =&gt; [
        15, // this means...
        20, // this means...
    ],
    'option_2' =&gt; [
        30, // this means...
        40, // this means...
        50, // this means...
    ],
    'option_3' =&gt; [
        99, // this means...
    ],
];

// your model's search method 
public function search(string $value, array $statusOptions = []): array
{
    $selectedStatuses = array_merge(
        ...array_values(
            array_intersect_key($this-&gt;optionStatusMap, $statusOptions)
        )
    );
    return $this-&gt;db
        -&gt;where_in('status', $selectedStatuses ?: null)
        -&gt;get_where('your_table', ['your_column' =&gt; $value])
        -&gt;result();
}
</code></pre>
<p>I am dividing your <code>$search</code> variable before the model. Have the <code>$search['value']</code> as the <code>$value</code> argument and the remaining <code>$search</code> elements as the <code>$statusOptions</code> argument.</p>
<p>Falling back to <code>null</code> in <code>where_in()</code> when the array is empty will prevent rendering an invalid query by omitting the <code>WHERE IN ()</code> expression.</p>
